## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/grunge_rust.html
- Summary (EN): Grunge Rust procedurally generates a rust-like texture by stacking several noise layers. Its Rust controls set how much of the surface is fully rusted, bare, or partly rusted, so it can serve as a mask for rust damage.
- Résumé (FR) : Grunge Rust génère une texture de rouille par empilement de bruits, avec des réglages de couverture, de douceur et de taille de paillettes.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata"]

- Key parameters: ["Range: Amplitude scales values before Center; Center offsets them; Mask Contrast increases extremes", "Pattern: Element Size, Element Scale (with Per-Component Controls), Offset, Tile Size in image coordinates", "Coverage: balance of fully rusted (white) and unrusted (black) areas", "Softness: how much partial rust shows under the fully rusted areas", "Rust: how much partial rust shows under the unrusted areas", "Rust Size: flake size; higher values give larger flakes", "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["Output can be negative or above 1 because layers store such values; use Clamp Minimum and Clamp Maximum", "Complement assumes values from 0 to 1", "The Contrast post-processing option differs from Noise Contrast on some noise nodes"]

